# Wallet security

- Treat any signing / key / approval-threshold change as high risk.
- Cursor may design flows and threat notes; Codex implements and audits by default.
- No private keys or mnemonics in logs, fixtures committed to git, or Telegram messages.
- Require multi-step confirmation for fund movement and guardian membership changes.
- Prefer allowlisted destinations and explicit amount limits when designing features.
